\to0
\end{equation*}
which is split by $\sigma':=p(\mathbb{R})^*\circ (r(\mathbb{R})^*)^{-1}$. 

Set $\alpha:=i_*$ and $\alpha':=i(\mathbb{R})_*$ and define $\beta:=\operatorname{Id}-(\sigma\circ j^*)$ and ${\beta':=\operatorname{Id}-(\sigma\circ j(\mathbb{R})^*)}$, so $\beta$ and $\beta'$ are the retractions of $\alpha$ and~$\alpha'$ induced by $\sigma$ and $\sigma'$. In the diagram
